d HHV-7 infections in PR pathogenesis.", "runs": [{"text": "Pityriasis rosea (PR) is an acute, self-limiting exanthematous disease that primarily affects children and young adults aged between 10 and 35 years. A large body of evidence supports the causal role of the endogenous systemic active human herpesvirus (HHV)-6 and HHV-7 infections in PR pathogenesis."}]}, {"id": "body-13256", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation:", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation:"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-13257", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Prodromal symptoms such as mild fever, sore throat, headache and loss of appetite", "runs": [{"text": "Prodromal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "such"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mild"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sore"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "throat,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "headache"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "loss"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "appetite"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1333"}}, {"id": "body-13258", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Begins with a \"herald\" or \"mother\" patch, a single round or oval lesion on the chest, neck, or back", "runs": [{"text": "Begins"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "\"herald\""}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "\"mother\""}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patch,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "single"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "round"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oval"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lesion"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chest,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "neck,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " back"}], "lis